# Where the Counter-Strike 2 weapon catalog comes from

Everything here was read on **2026-10-24** (decision **D473**). `catalog.json` is the
single-kind form (`kind: "weapons"`), **held for the owner's review** (`review`,
D132): nothing of it reaches a Core's AI Scripts until he deletes that line.

CS2 is a PC game (Steam), so this game is mainly for **Native Keyboard & Mouse**
(a real keyboard and mouse reach the game, the AI scripts run on top), not for a
console. Valve makes and publishes it.

## The list: the game's own files

The names, classes and sides are the game's own, read from the owner's CS2 install
(`D:\SteamLibrary\steamapps\common\Counter-Strike Global Offensive`, build
**2000559**, PatchVersion 1.40.8.6, 2025-07-07) with a small VPK reader
(Model Library `Counter-Strike 2/tools/vpkread.py`; nothing downloaded, nothing run
from the game):

- `scripts/items/items_game.txt` (in `pak01_dir.vpk`): every `weapon_*` item, its
  `item_type_name` (the class), `used_by_classes` (which team can buy it), its
  `item_gear_slot` and its in-game price.
- `resource/csgo_english.txt`: each item's `item_name` string, which is exactly
  what the HUD prints under the weapon's icon ("AK-47", "SG 553", "Zeus x27",
  "High Explosive Grenade").

**Is that build current?** Valve's patch notes (Steam's official announcements for
app 730, `https://store.steampowered.com/news/app/730`, read through
`api.steampowered.com/ISteamNews/GetNewsForApp`) from 2025-07-02 to 2026-10-22 add
**no weapon**, remove none, rename none and change no side. They change prices only:
**2026-01-21** MP7 and MP5-SD $100 cheaper, PP-Bizon $100 cheaper. New finishes,
collections and stickers are skins on the same weapons and change nothing here.
So the list is complete for 2026-10-24.

**65 items in 10 groups**, every one with a picture:

- 10 pistols, 7 SMGs, 4 shotguns, 2 machine guns, 7 rifles, 4 sniper rifles: both
  teams' buy menus (Pistols, Mid-Tier and Rifles tabs).
- 6 grenades (Utility), the Zeus x27 and the Medi-Shot (Equipment; the Medi-Shot is
  bought in no competitive mode, it is given in Deathmatch and some community
  modes; kept because the HUD names it).
- 22 knives: the two default knives (CT and T; the HUD calls both "Knife") and the
  20 knife models the game holds. A knife with a finish prints with a star
  ("★ Karambit | Doppler").
- the C4 (slot 5, Terrorists only).

**Not weapons:** Kevlar Vest, Kevlar + Helmet, the Defuse Kit and the Rescue Kit are
bought in the Utility tab but are never held, so no Script can tie to them. The
Gun Game knife (`weapon_knifegg`), the bump mine, the breach charge, the tablet,
the shield, the fists, the axe, the hammer, the spanner and the snowball are
Danger Zone / retired items no current mode hands out; they are not listed.

### Ids, aliases, fire modes, sides

- Ids are `<group>.<slug of the HUD name>` (README.md), except the two default
  knives, `knives.knife_ct` and `knives.knife_t` (one HUD name, two models).
- `aliases`: the names players use (Scout, Deag, Krieg, CT auto); search only.
- `fireMode`: `auto`, `semi`, `bolt` (AWP, SSG 08), `pump` (Nova, Sawed-Off,
  MAG-7). The Glock-18 and the FAMAS have a burst switch (right mouse button);
  they are marked by their default (`semi`, `auto`).
- `side` (new, D473): which team can BUY it: `ct`, `t` or `both`. Either team can
  PICK UP any gun, so `side` is the buy-phase prior of the round memory only
  (recognition.json), never a filter on what is read.

