## Pictures: Valve's own renders from the game files (owner, 2026-10-24)

Every picture in `weapons/` is the game's own base weapon render (the one the game's
inventory and loadout screens draw for a weapon with no finish), read from the
owner's CS2 install: `pak01_dir.vpk`, `panorama/images/econ/weapons/base_weapons/
<weapon>_png.vtex_c`, a 512 x 384 BGRA8888 texture, decoded (LZ4 mips) by
Model Library `Counter-Strike 2/tools/vtex.py`, cropped to the weapon (transparent
border removed, 4 px kept) and fitted to 480 x 300, transparency kept.

**This is Valve art (flagged).** The owner decided on 2026-10-24 to use the real
official CS2 weapon art and handle the licence himself ("licensing isn't a
blocker"). No Valve web page we found publishes these base renders, so each
picture's source is the exact game file it came from (the test accepts a
`cs2-vpk:` path for Valve, `test-game-data.js` PUBLISHERS). Nothing came from a
fan wiki, a skin site or an image search, and none is generated. Delete a `.png`
and set that weapon's `image` to `null` and the app shows the class symbol.

